{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/beatUnit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/beatunit"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLMetronomeV12BeatUnitTiedV04beatE0AA16MXLNoteKindValueOvp","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"beatUnit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}],"title":"beatUnit"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat-unit element indicates the graphical note type to use in a metronome mark."}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"beatUnit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<beat-unit>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied/beatUnit":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied\/beatUnit","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied\/beatunit","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"beatUnit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL16MXLNoteKindValueO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}],"title":"beatUnit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat-unit element indicates the graphical note type to use in a metronome mark."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNoteKindValue":{"title":"MXLNoteKindValue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLNoteKindValue"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotekindvalue","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNoteKindValue","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNoteKindValue","abstract":[{"text":"The note-type-value type is used for the MusicXML type element and represents the graphic note type, from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1024th (shortest) to maxima (longest).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/BeatUnitTied":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/BeatUnitTied","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BeatUnitTied"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/beatunittied","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BeatUnitTied"}],"title":"MXLMetronome.BeatUnitTied","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The beat-unit-tied type indicates a beat-unit within a metronome mark that is tied to the preceding beat-unit."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This allows two or more tied notes to be associated with a per-minute value in a metronome mark, whereas the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome-tied element is restricted to metric relationship marks."}],"type":"topic"}}}